---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Reveal from '../components/Reveal.astro';
import { company } from '../data/site';

/**
 * Accessibility statement.
 *
 * URL deliberately matches the original site: /accessibility-statement.
 *
 * The original page was an UNEDITED Wix template — it still contained the
 * template's own authoring instructions ("this page currently has two
 * sections, once editing is complete one section needs to be deleted").
 * Rather than carry that across, this page states what is actually true of
 * this build, all of which was verified rather than asserted:
 *   - every text/background pair measured against WCAG AA contrast
 *   - one h1 per page, no heading-level skips
 *   - all links and buttons carry accessible names
 *   - skip link reachable on first Tab
 *   - prefers-reduced-motion honoured
 *   - no horizontal scroll at 375 / 768 / 1440 px
 *
 * Keep it honest: if a claim here stops being true, change the claim.
 */
const lastUpdated = 'August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility Statement"
  description="Urjapod Energy is committed to making this website accessible to everyone, including people with disabilities. This statement describes the measures taken and how to report a problem."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Accessibility"
    title="Accessibility statement"
    lead="We want everyone to be able to use this site, including people who browse with a keyboard, a screen reader, magnification, or with motion sensitivity."
  />

  <Section width="narrow">
    <Reveal>
      <Prose>
        <h2>Our commitment</h2>
        <p>
          Urjapod Energy is working to make this website accessible to people
          with disabilities. An accessible site lets visitors with disabilities
          browse with the same level of ease and enjoyment as everyone else. We
          treat accessibility as part of building the site, not as something
          added afterwards.
        </p>

        <h2>What we have done</h2>
        <p>
          This site was built to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines
          (WCAG) 2.1 Level AA. Specifically:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Colour contrast.</strong> Every text and background
            combination on the site was measured, not estimated, and meets or
            exceeds the 4.5:1 ratio required for normal text.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Keyboard access.</strong> Every link, button and form field
            can be reached and operated with a keyboard alone. Focus outlines
            are never removed, and a “Skip to content” link is the first thing
            you reach when you press Tab.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Structure.</strong> Each page has a single main heading and
            a heading order that does not skip levels, so screen reader users
            can navigate by headings. Landmarks (header, main, footer,
            navigation) are marked up so they can be jumped between.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Names for controls.</strong> Every link and button has a
            meaningful accessible name. Icons that carry meaning are labelled;
            purely decorative graphics are hidden from assistive technology so
            they are not read out as noise.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Reduced motion.</strong> If your operating system is set to
            reduce motion, all animation and smooth scrolling on this site is
            switched off automatically.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Zoom and small screens.</strong> Text can be enlarged
            without breaking the layout, pinch-zoom is not disabled, and no
            page scrolls sideways at common screen widths.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Forms.</strong> Fields have visible labels rather than
            placeholder-only hints, errors are described in text next to the
            field they belong to, and focus moves to the first problem when a
            submission fails.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Works without JavaScript.</strong> All content and contact
            details remain readable if scripts fail to load. Only the contact
            form requires JavaScript, and our email address and phone number
            are shown as plain text beside it.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Known limitations</h2>
        <p>
          We would rather name the gaps than claim there are none:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The battery chemistry comparison table on the Technology page is
            wider than a phone screen and scrolls sideways within its own
            frame. It is reachable by keyboard and labelled as a scrollable
            region, but a wide table remains harder to read on a small screen
            than on a large one.
          </li>
          <li>
            This site has not yet been audited by an independent accessibility
            specialist, nor formally tested with every screen reader and
            browser combination.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Tell us if something does not work</h2>
        <p>
          If you find any part of this site difficult or impossible to use, we
          want to hear about it — it is the fastest way for us to fix it.
          Please email <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>
          or call <a href={`tel:${company.phoneHref}`}>{company.phone}</a>, and
          tell us the page and what went wrong. We will reply and let you know
          how we intend to put it right.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you need any information from this site in a different format,
          contact us and we will provide it.
        </p>

        <h2>This statement</h2>
        <p>
          This statement applies to <strong>www.urjapod.com</strong> and was
          last reviewed in {lastUpdated}. It describes the accessibility of the
          site as built; we review it when the site changes.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </Reveal>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
